<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antigua Labour Party</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Antigua and Barbuda Labour Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Antigua Labour Party, later renamed the Antigua and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbuda">Barbuda</a> Labour Party, grew out of the Antigua Trades and Labour Union in the 1940s. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vere-bird">Vere Bird</a> and later his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lester-bird">Lester Bird</a> it dominated Antiguan politics, leading the country to independence in 1981 and governing until 2004. It returned to power under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaston-browne">Gaston Browne</a> in 2014.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antigua-labour-party.jpg" alt="Antigua Labour Party" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LadyofHats, based on a bitmap by Ralf Hartemink · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Antigua_and_Barbuda.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
